= March 2025 — Defend the ruling or legislate the right

The Supreme Court has removed the requirement for trans people to sue their
parents when seeking legal gender recognition. The ruling simplifies the
procedure, but Parliament can still establish a clearer statutory right and
consistent rules for courts and registries.

- @gender_statute
- @gender_guidance
- @gender_opposition_toolkit
- @gender_quiet

